The bundled copies of zlib, libpng, libjpeg, libmng and sqlite (2.x) were
removed; Qt is built against the system libraries instead (-system-zlib,
-system-libpng, -system-libjpeg, -system-libmng).

The SQLite driver was removed together with the bundled sqlite, as it only
supports SQLite 2.x.

What is left here:

    opentype - OpenType layout code used by the X11 font engine
               (part of Qt's text shaping, not a standalone library)
